Feature: Guarded program loops propose and existing checkers decide
  All checks cover the complete declared input domain and exact eager failures.
  No loop grants owner, adoption, publication or deployment authority.

  @atdd-loop-pipeline
  Scenario: Complete and repair proposals before optimizing qualified programs
    Given an immutable original, a bound proposal and a sequence from the fixed stage grammar
    When the pipeline completes holes or repairs a checker-refuted expression
    Then every emitted program passes transform check with its receipt replayed before qualification
    And a skipped guard never supplies a candidate or a checker verdict
    And eager dead-node overflow cannot be removed without a counterexample
    And a later budget stop returns inconclusive with no attempt and no candidate export

  @atdd-loop-strategy
  Scenario: Freeze the winning development strategy before evaluation
    Given distinct development and evaluation subjects bound by complete original program content
    When the meta-loop enumerates the fixed guarded stage grammar within its shared budget
    Then it compares qualified development counts, program nodes and gate pair allowances
    And it freezes the winner before any evaluation search or check
    And changing evaluation proposals cannot change that selection
    And renaming a development subject cannot create an evaluation holdout
    And an incomplete development search returns inconclusive without selecting a winner

  @atdd-loop-rules
  Scenario: Recheck concrete learned rules and every rewritten whole program
    Given concrete typed terms partitioned by exact complete finite meanings
    When the rule door proposes cheaper representatives and reuses a bank on a target domain
    Then each rule is rechecked by transform check with matched receipt replay on that target
    And every changed whole program is checked against the fixed original with replay
    And a forged bank and a source-only identity cannot authorize a rewrite
    And a whole-program eager trap survives when term equivalence alone would remove it
    And the independent reference detects planted partition and program faults
    And its self-test fails when the comparison is stubbed
